<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: CZECH SEPAP CZK 188.4MLN CONSOLIDATED NET - IAS.</title>
<headline>CZECH SEPAP CZK 188.4MLN CONSOLIDATED NET - IAS.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1996-11-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Consolidated results, calculated</p>
<p>according to international accounting standards (IAS), for</p>
<p>nine-month period ending September 30, 1996: (in millions of</p>
<p>crowns)</p>
<p> Net profit	   188.380    vs    520.431</p>
<p> Pre-tax profit     165.265    vs    867.244</p>
<p> Gross profit     2,137.494    vs  2,962.822</p>
<p> Sales		4,197.133    vs   5,444.445</p>
<p> Revenues	   3,944.739    vs   5,338.789</p>
<p> Tax credit	   -29.959    vs     346.813</p>
<p>Provision for</p>
<p>  income tax	    5.844    vs	  0</p>
<p>Note. Full company name is Sepap Group a.s., a paper and</p>
<p>forest products concern. Its two main shareholders are</p>
<p>Daventree Ltd, controlled by Bahamas-based investor Michael</p>
<p>Dingman (48 percent), and Swedish forestry concern Assidoman AS</p>
<p>(39 percent).</p>
<p>-- Prague Newsroom, 42-2-2423-0003</p>
</text>
